{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.LiftFromReality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LiftFromReality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Block","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeLiftInterface"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LiftFromReality.equal_split_of_real_operator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LiftFromReality.equal_split_of_real_operator","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LiftFromReality.lean#L106-L115","doc":"With the constructor in hand, the conditional measure conclusions of the\ninterface apply to any real self-adjoint loop operator: its two Hodge-block\nweights split equally — the ½ of `½·a₀`, end to end. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LiftFromReality.tauRhoHodgeLift_of_real_operator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LiftFromReality.tauRhoHodgeLift_of_real_operator","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LiftFromReality.lean#L93-L104","doc":"**The instance constructor (the honest discharge path).** Any hermitian\noperator on the doubled space commuting with the swap-conjugation induces a\nlegitimate `TauRhoHodgeLift` on its diagonal blocks — both class fields are\nPROVED from the reality premise. The open wall is exactly the premise: that\nthe actual α_EM loop weight operator on `H¹(Bring)` is such an operator with\n`H^{1,0}`-block the τ-image of the canonical Markov channel weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LiftFromReality.hermitian_block_of_isHermitian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LiftFromReality.hermitian_block_of_isHermitian","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LiftFromReality.lean#L85-L91","doc":"Self-adjointness of the full operator passes to the `H^{1,0}` block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LiftFromReality.conjugated_of_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LiftFromReality.conjugated_of_real","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LiftFromReality.lean#L75-L82","doc":"**Reality forces the `conjugated` field.** If the full operator commutes\nwith the swap-conjugation (`C M C = M`), its lower diagonal block is the\nentrywise conjugate of its upper diagonal block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LiftFromReality.swap_conj_blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LiftFromReality.swap_conj_blocks","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LiftFromReality.lean#L58-L73","doc":"Conjugating a block operator by the swap-conjugation `C`: matrix form\n`P · (M.map star) · P` exchanges the diagonal blocks and conjugates entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LiftFromReality.swapP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LiftFromReality.swapP","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LiftFromReality.lean#L53-L56","doc":"The block swap `P` on the doubled space `V ⊕ V̄` — the linear part of the\nantilinear swap-conjugation `C(x,y) = (ȳ, x̄)` (matrix form: `C = P ∘ conj`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}